const gatePrompt = `You are the integration gate for the zz tmux-compat campaign (repo demfabris/zz, board = GitHub issue 7). All workers and reviewers are done; you run ALONE on this ${M.machine}, full speed. FOREGROUND ONLY: run every command in the foreground (a plain Bash call with a timeout; split long scenario batches into several calls); never use Monitor, run_in_background or any background task, and never end your turn to wait for one; you are done only when you have emitted the structured report (merges, progress_after, board_updates, attached_client, problems). Integrate IN THIS ORDER: client first (the possible v100 bump: zz-protocol, zz-daemon status.rs, zz-client, zz-tui, crates/zz tests and the clipboard arm, status-row.sh, tui-pane-geometry.sh, its fixtures), mux second (zz-mux command.rs, daemon.rs's if-shell and run-shell insertion path, its scenarios). One gate per branch, and push main as soon as each lane's gate is green (if you die mid-run the orchestrator resumes from what already landed). A branch whose diff touches nothing under crates/ (git diff --stat origin/main...HEAD) skips stages 3a and 3b and runs 3c and 3d only, with the delta corpus taken as every scenario it added or changed plus the whole attached fixture. The summaries below carry each lane's worker report and its review verdict; a lane may have been rejected once and fixed by a fresh agent on the same branch, in which case review is the re-review and first_review the original.

Lane summaries, worker report + Opus 5 review verdict each:
${JSON.stringify(summaries, null, 2)}

REVIEW VERDICTS BIND YOU: approve-with-fixes => apply every must-fix on the branch (own follow-up commit) before its gate, re-running the reviewer's failing probe to prove each fix. reject => do NOT merge; post the blockers as a board note on the lock front, leave the branch, continue. A blocker you can genuinely fix in minutes may be fixed and merged with the probe re-run as proof; a wrong close whose revert applies cleanly is such a fix (precedent 0fec342 + 9cab1fa: revert, then a records commit that puts the reviewer's measurement into the group reason and acceptance). review_actions must account for every confirmed defect. Missing review (null) => do a compressed contract audit yourself before gating. If you SKIP a lane, push its rebased-and-fixed tip to origin as campaign/<name>-gated before removing the worktree.

BOARD IDENTITY: ZZ_BOARD_HOLDER=${M.holder} python3 compat/board.py <cmd> from inside a repo checkout. Verbs: release/withdraw REQUIRE --reason; note takes --note; candidate takes --commit --branch --base + repeatable --proof; integrated takes --merge + optional --gate; renew <FRONT> --lease 2h (always give a unit); front needs --contract --zones [--priority <int> --kind --deps --notes]; withdraw and front need TRIAGE held; integrated needs MAIN held. The orchestrator holds the two lock fronts F-TUI-CLIENT-CLOSE (client lane) and F-MUX-BUFFER-IFSHELL (mux lane) (14h leases from launch; expired => claim back as ${M.holder} before that lane's ledger step). BOARD FALLBACK: if a board command fails on GitHub authentication, append the exact command line you meant to run to ${M.root}/compat/orchestration/board-replay-18.sh (do not commit that file), say so in board_updates, and continue the gate; the orchestrator replays the file. Never let a board failure stop a merge.

${M.gitNote} Fetch git fetch origin +refs/heads/main:refs/remotes/origin/main '+refs/heads/campaign/*:refs/remotes/origin/campaign/*'; push git push origin HEAD:main. The shared checkout ${M.root} is where you start; its local main branch is stale; never use it, never edit it, never stash or reset in it.
knowledge/tmux/gaps.md is generated: regenerate with tmux-tracker.py write-report on every conflict, never hand-merge it.
PROTOCOL RECONCILE: ONLY the client lane may have bumped 99 -> 100 (its notes say whether its last group landed), and it merges first, so the mux branch rebases onto a tree whose wire types may have changed. A compile break on such a rebase (a new StatusLine field the mux branch constructs in a test, a renamed helper) is yours to fix in the rebase, in a follow-up commit, with the lane's package tests re-run; a wire-reachable change in the mux branch is a finding: if the client lane bumped, reconcile it INTO the single v100 changelog (one constant at 100, one hunt_claims fixture at 0x64, every bullet preserved) and verify cargo test -p zz-protocol after; if nothing bumped, it is a blocker and the mux branch is skipped. catalog.rs counters, the option-consumer roster and compat_manifest_tests.rs counts conflict between lanes routinely: resolve by recounting, then cargo test -p zz-mux and -p zz-protocol, and grep the tree for conflict markers before building. The lanes touch compat/tmux-gaps.json in declared, disjoint records (${OWNERSHIP}); when a rebase conflicts there, ${M.root}/compat/orchestration/gaps-merge.py BASE OURS THEIRS OUT merges the two sides by record id and exits 2 on a record both sides changed differently (feed it git show :1:compat/tmux-gaps.json, :2:, :3:), then regenerate gaps.md and recount. compat/results/summary.md conflicts are row unions: keep every row from both sides, sorted as the file is; a row both sides changed (none expected) is recounted by running that scenario once; the Recorded at footer stays whatever main has until step 7. daemon.rs may be touched by both lanes in disjoint functions (the status publication by the client lane, the if-shell insertion by the mux lane): keep both.

THIS BOX: ${M.boxNote} Use ONE shared build directory for every gate worktree, export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=${M.dev}/zz-gate-target in every shell that runs cargo, compat/check.sh included (gates are serial, so it is never contended; leave the directory in place for the next cycle). target/debug/zz there is whichever worktree built last: cargo build -p zz in the worktree under test before spawning any binary from it, every time. Never touch ${M.protected}. Before gating a branch, run git merge-tree --write-tree origin/main <tip> first; it predicts the conflicts and costs one command. Every zz you start outside the harness reads ~/.tmux.conf; the box has a real one (the user's), so your own probes and the full run's servers must keep HOME scrubbed or pass -f /dev/null exactly as the harness does; never let a gate server load the user's file.

PER BRANCH, in order:
1. Fresh worktree: git -C ${M.root} worktree add ${M.root}-gate-<key> origin/main (remove leftovers with --force first). Rebase branch onto origin/main; compat/tmux-gaps.json conflicts between lanes are normal: merge both sides.
2. First branch only: claim MAIN --lease 6h; hold across all, renew before each subsequent gate, release after the ledger recompute.
3. Code-branch gate stages, in order:
   a. timeout 2400 cargo test --workspace --all-features --no-fail-fast --jobs ${M.gateJobs} -- --test-threads=${M.gateThreads} > log 2>&1 (check exit code; never pipe through tail). Timeout-guard: wait_exit_holds_the_control_process_until_a_second_blank_line can HANG under load; if the run wedges >20min with no output, sample the process; a lost-wakeup hang there counts as the known flake (verify solo).
   b. cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings, AND cargo clippy -p zz-tui --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings (green since cycle 17; a gate stage).
   c. ${RUN_ENV} compat/run.sh --strict-geometry --delta origin/main..HEAD --commands <lane touched_commands>. Run --list TWICE and reconcile against git diff --name-only for compat/scenarios; for the client lane ADD every keys, mouse, copy, clipboard, chooser, popup, menu, status and refresh scenario plus the attached fixture, compat/status-row.sh and compat/tui-pane-geometry.sh (both must EXIT 0 at the client tip: the stdin stall closes the geometry tool's wait and the detach hint decision closes the status row's last comparison); for the mux lane ADD every buffer, if-shell, run-shell, source-file, config and plugin-runtime scenario plus the attached fixture. Shard up to ${M.shards} concurrent run.sh invocations over DISJOINT scenario subsets with separate result logs (compat/run.sh hard-codes RESULTS_DIR, so shards stay apart only by disjoint scenario names); give each shard a timeout and run smoke/source-replay-diagnostics and smoke/pane-border-lines SOLO after the shards (pin-side crash and a hang under load respectively); any divergence re-runs alone before being called real.
   d. python3 compat/tmux-tracker.py check && python3 compat/board_test.py && compat/check.sh. Then compat/run.sh --check-summary: a scenario-inventory diff is a lane defect (fix the rows, they are a row union). KNOWN AND EXPECTED: a branch that changed compat/attached-client.sh after the 6edc5c7ec425 stamp fails --check-summary BY CONSTRUCTION with "attached-client PASS ... predates changes to the fixture itself"; the crates/ drift warning is the same class. Neither is a lane defect and neither is a reason to skip a branch: treat that exact failure as green for stage d, merge, and let step 7's stamped full run re-record the footer at the merged tip.
4. Flake rules: lone timing test failing loaded + passing exact-solo = flake, proceed (known list: copy-mode reconcile, client_focus_closes… (also fails about one solo run in three; two solo passes of three count), event_hooks_fire_after_mutation_with_captured_formats, history_request_is_guarded…, daemon_native_split_resize_commits_exactly…, nested_alias_queue_bubbles_shutdown…, control_sourced_run_shell_closes_before_raw_output…, request_full_enqueues_only_the_requested_visible_pane, display_menu_resize_lifecycle::a_resize_moves_the_menu…, zz-terminal pty_output_drains_while_the_input_writer_is_backpressured, wait_exit… hang, concurrent_default_interactive… "not a terminal" incl. misattribution, behavior-options one TOPO row under shard load, smoke/pane-border-lines hang under shard load, smoke/vim-tmux-navigator keys rows under load). Anything else red = real: fix if minutes, else SKIP branch (no push to main; push the gated tip as campaign/<name>-gated), record, continue.
5. Push main. Non-fast-forward: fetch; user-authored commits + conflict-free disjoint rebase => bounded rerun (lane package tests + its scenarios), push. Never force. Campaign branches rewritten by the rebase stay at their old tips on origin (never force them); say so in the report.
6. Ledger per successful push against that lane's lock_front: candidate (--commit tip --branch campaign/<name> --base <pre-push main> --proof per stage), note (--note: groups covered, slugs closed/relocated, decisions recorded, reviewer verdict + what you did about defects), integrated (--merge <sha> --gate "workspace+clippy+delta green"), release (--reason "batch integrated at <sha>"). A lane that left one of its groups open gets integrated + a release whose --reason names what is still open.
7. After ALL branches, holding MAIN, in the last gate worktree at the pushed main tip: THE STAMPED FULL RUN. cargo build -p zz (CARGO_TARGET_DIR as above, so zz and zz_cli sit at ${M.dev}/zz-gate-target/debug), then ${RUN_ENV} ZZ_COMPAT_ZZ=${M.dev}/zz-gate-target/debug/zz timeout 9000 compat/run.sh --attached-client > log 2>&1 with HOME scrubbed. IT TAKES ABOUT 70 MINUTES on this box (cycle 16's first attempt died at scenario 137 on a 48-minute inner timeout and had to restart from zero): give it that 9000-second bound, start it once, and wait on it with bounded foreground polling calls (sleep-and-tail loops of a few minutes each, checking the process is alive), never a second start. On PASS it rewrites compat/results/summary.md with Recorded at: <sha>. If the fixture fails, re-run it once solo (compat/attached-client.sh <zz> <pin tmux>); if it fails again, name the probe in attached_client, leave the summary as it was, and do NOT hand-edit a PASS. A dying run leaves zz daemons on /tmp/zza-*.sock: reap them by pid from the socket name, never by pkill -f. If a corpus row (not the fixture) fails at the merged tip, that is a regression one of the lanes introduced: fix it if minutes, else report it. ALSO at the merged tip run compat/status-row.sh and compat/tui-pane-geometry.sh once with the rebuilt zz and record their exit codes and output in attached_client; if either is not 0, the corresponding close is unproved at the merged tip and the records commit must say so in the group reason (reopen the item rather than bank it). Then recompute TMUX_COMPAT_TRACKER.md from the merged registry: the headline lines (Campaign delivery; Live work "<open> OPEN + <blocked> BLOCKED = <sum>" counting the post-freeze groups honestly; Ledger settlement; Exit evidence with the scenario and step counts and the stamped attached-client PASS or its failure), the Orchestration line (cycle 18 integrated on the ubuntu box on Claude Code Opus 5 lanes at xhigh, client then mux, one gate alone), the Current checkpoint rows, the Campaign dashboard table rows (Live unresolved, Latest differential, Differential SHA-256 = sha256 of compat/results/summary.md, Ledger settlement, Live registry counts), and a new "### ${M.date} cycle-18 integration checkpoint" table like the cycle-17 one above it. ALSO refresh the bundle pages that carry live registry and corpus numbers, listed under "Pages that carry live checkpoint numbers" in compat/orchestration/HANDOFF.md, and knowledge/protocol pages if a v100 bump left a stale v99 mention anywhere (grep), and append a "### ${M.date} cycle-18 integration" entry to compat/orchestration/CAMPAIGN-LOG.md in the shape of the cycle-17 one (what merged, what stayed open, what the reviews caught and whether a fix pass ran, the stamp). Records commit ("Recompute the live ledger after the cycle-18 merges", including the stamped summary.md), then compat/run.sh --check-summary MUST print "summary current" on that commit, push, ledger it as integrated MAIN --merge <sha>, release MAIN.
8. Claim TRIAGE. Withdraw fronts fully mooted by the merges (none expected besides the lane locks; the F-SPLIT-MUX-*-V5 chain stays). If a worker's skip reasons prove a group contract is unprovable as written, post that as a residual on the relevant front. If the registry still holds open items after this cycle, post one residual on TRIAGE listing each with its owner and what the merged tip measures. If instead every post-freeze group is done (python3 compat/progress.py lists no open post-freeze group and gaps[] holds only accepted groups), say so in board_updates and post a note on TRIAGE that the campaign's registry is closed; F-GUI-MENU-MOUSE-MODALITY stays READY as a design front either way. Release TRIAGE.
9. python3 compat/progress.py, full output, into progress_after.
10. Remove only your own ${M.root}-gate-* worktrees (after pushing any skipped lane's gated tip). Leave zz-lane-* and zz-review-*.

Never stash/reset anything in ${M.root}. Never kill tmux or zz servers you did not start (${M.protected}). Report per branch merged/sha/gate_summary/review_actions/flakes, full progress output, board records, the attached-client outcome, problems.`

const gate = summaries.length
  ? await agent(gatePrompt, { label: 'gate:serial', phase: 'Integrate', schema: GATE_SCHEMA, ...OPTS })
  : null
if (!gate) log('No branches to integrate: all workers came back empty.')

return { lanes: laneResults, gate }
